{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_017","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"# Load data from a file.\n var err = config.load(\"user://scores.cfg\")","location_hint":"paragraph 27","char_start":1998,"char_end":2066,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_018","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"# If the file didn't load, ignore it.\n if err != OK:\n return","location_hint":"paragraph 28","char_start":2069,"char_end":2129,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_019","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"# Iterate over all sections.\n for player in config.get_sections():\n # Fetch the data for each section.\n var player_name = config.get_value(player, \"player_name\")\n var player_score = config.get_value(player, \"best_score\")\n score_data[player_name] = player_score","location_hint":"paragraph 29","char_start":2132,"char_end":2392,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_020","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"var score_data = new Godot.Collections.Dictionary();\n var config = new ConfigFile();","location_hint":"paragraph 31","char_start":2418,"char_end":2502,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_021","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"// Load data from a file.\n Error err = config.Load(\"user://scores.cfg\");","location_hint":"paragraph 32","char_start":2505,"char_end":2577,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_022","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"// If the file didn't load, ignore it.\n if (err != Error.Ok)\n {\n return;\n }","location_hint":"paragraph 33","char_start":2580,"char_end":2655,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_023","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"// Iterate over all sections.\n foreach (String player in config.GetSections())\n {\n // Fetch the data for each section.\n var player_name = (String)config.GetValue(player, \"player_name\");\n var player_score = (int)config.GetValue(player, \"best_score\");\n score_data[player_name] = player_score;\n }","location_hint":"paragraph 34","char_start":2658,"char_end":2951,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_024","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"Any operation that mutates the ConfigFile such as :ref:`set_value()<class_ConfigFile_method_set_value>`, :ref:`clear()<class_ConfigFile_method_clear>`, or :ref:`erase_section()<class_ConfigFile_method_erase_section>`, only changes what is loaded in memory. If you want to write the change to a file, you have to save the changes with :ref:`save()<class_ConfigFile_method_save>`, :ref:`save_encrypted()<class_ConfigFile_method_save_encrypted>`, or :ref:`save_encrypted_pass()<class_ConfigFile_method_save_encrypted_pass>`.","location_hint":"paragraph 35","char_start":2953,"char_end":3474,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_025","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"Keep in mind that section and property names can't contain spaces. Anything after a space will be ignored on save and on load.","location_hint":"paragraph 36","char_start":3476,"char_end":3602,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d02146dfcea5_026","source_id":"src_d02146dfcea5","source_hash":"05a1727494d21181b9e20fe814644f0f105df2d1aebbb9a408e361f43a7a171d","text":"ConfigFiles can also contain manually written comment lines starting with a semicolon (``;``). Those lines will be ignored when parsing the file. Note that comments will be lost when saving the ConfigFile. This can still be useful for dedicated server configuration files, which are typically never overwritten without explicit user action.","location_hint":"paragraph 37","char_start":3604,"char_end":3944,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:11:34.958Z"}
